# UAT suite configuration. Copy to .env.uat and adjust per target.
# This file is committed; .env.uat is not. Never put a secret in either —
# the suite holds no credentials by design (see below).

# ── Target ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend deployment under test. The backend is reached through this
# origin's /api/* proxy, so it is never configured separately.
UAT_BASE_URL=https://orizons.xyz

# Stellar network this target is EXPECTED to report at /api/stellar/network.
# Asserted, not assumed: a mismatch fails the entry-criteria check rather than
# silently testing the wrong chain. See defect D-001.
UAT_EXPECTED_NETWORK=testnet

# ── Notes on credentials ──────────────────────────────────
# The suite deliberately holds NO secrets:
#
#   * No wallet key. Nothing in UAT signs a transaction. Wallet-gated UI is
#     reached with a localStorage session stub (tests/fixtures.ts), which
#     satisfies the app's "is a wallet connected" check without granting the
#     ability to sign.
#
#   * No X-API-Key. The API-key-gated routes are probed for REFUSAL only.
#     Holding an operator key would let a UAT run move real fiat through the
#     PDAX routes, which is exactly what UAT must never do.
#
# If a future criterion genuinely needs a credential, add it here as an empty
# documented variable and inject it from CI secrets — never commit a value.
